    <string name="tools_summary">Calibrate, reset peaks</string>
    <string name="tools_hint">Calibrate makes the app learn the phone\'s position again; it normally does this by itself. Reset peaks clears the highest G values for this car.</string>
    <string name="guide_step_mount">Fix the phone in a mount. Any angle works, as long as it doesn\'t move.</string>
    <string name="guide_step_source">Choose where speed comes from under Speed source. Phone GPS needs nothing extra.</string>
    <string name="guide_step_drive">Drive. Speed shows straight away. G-force appears after the app has felt the car speed up, brake and turn, usually within half a minute.</string>
    <string name="guide_step_focus">Tap the speed gauge or the G circle to fill the screen with it. Tap again to see both.</string>
    <string name="guide_step_record">To keep a drive, open Drives and tap Record drive, then stop when you arrive. Then tap Open on map under Saved drives to see it in Google Earth.</string>
    <string name="guide_note">If you pick up or move the phone, G-force pauses and comes back by itself.</string>
    <string name="drives_hint">Each drive you record is saved here with its path, speed and G-force. Open on map shows it in Google Earth, which must be installed: the path coloured by speed, the hard pushes marked, a fly-along tour that shows each hard push, and a speed wall to switch on in 3D. Share KML or GPX sends the file to a computer or another map app. Drives stay on this phone until you share one.</string>
